1
00:00:00,310 --> 00:00:01,630
(Sheldon:)Hardly.

2
00:00:01,630 --> 00:00:04,330
(Sheldon:)Consider this unlikely
but very plausible scenario.

3
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:07,070
(Sheldon:)A young woman alone
in the big city.

4
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:08,470
(Sheldon:)Her ridiculous dream

5
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:11,270
(Sheldon:)of becoming an actress
lies shattered about her.

6
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,840
(Penny:)Hey, wait a minute.

7
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:14,810
(Howard:)Well, hang on. Let's
see where he's going.

8
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:16,250
(Sheldon:)Then it hits her.

9
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:18,010
(Sheldon:)How is she going to survive?

10
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:21,530
(Sheldon:)I mean, she has no prospects,
no marketable skills.

11
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,000
(Sheldon:)And then one day,

12
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,120
(Sheldon:)she meets a group of geniuses

13
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:27,060
(Sheldon:)and their friend Howard.

14
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,930
(Howard:)Hey, I...

15
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:32,900
(Howard:)Hang on.
Let's see where he's going.

16
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,630
(Sheldon:)She befriends them,
and then lies in wait

17
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:39,270
(Sheldon:)until they reveal
a marketable idea,

18
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:42,210
(Sheldon:)which she steals
and sells to the highest bidder.

19
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:44,340
- That is ridiculous.
- Oh, is it?

20
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:45,940
(Sheldon:)Let's see you come up
with an explanation

21
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:48,650
(Sheldon:)as to why this woman hangs out
with us all the time.

22
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:53,980
(Penny:)Oh, great. You know what?

23
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:55,570
(Penny:)I've already mooched
dinner off you guys.

24
00:00:55,570 --> 00:00:56,920
(Penny:)I don't need to listen to this.

25
00:00:56,920 --> 00:01:00,020
(Howard:)There's your answer--
free food.

